# minimum Qore version
%requires qore >= 2.0

# require type definitions everywhere

# enable all warnings
%modern
%allow-weak-references

%requires HttpServerUtil
%requires Util
%requires(reexport) Logger
%requires Mime

%try-module json >= 1.5
%define NoJson
%endtry

module ServerSentEventHandler {
    version = "1.0.2";
    desc = "User module for handling SSE connections";
    author = "David Nichols <david@qore.org>";
    url = "http://qore.org";
    license = "MIT";
}

/** @mainpage ServerSentEventHandler Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section serversenteventhandlerintro Introduction to the ServerSentEventHandler Module

    The %ServerSentEventHandler module provides a handler to be used with the
    <a href="../../HttpServer/html/index.html">HttpServer module</a> to provide
    <a href="ç">Server-Sent Event</a> connections.

    To use this module, use \c "%requires ServerSentEventHandler" and \c "%requires HttpServer" in your code.

    All the public symbols in the module are defined in the ServerSentEventHandler namespace.

    The main classes provided in this module are:
    - @ref ServerSentEventHandler::ServerSentEventConnection
    - @ref ServerSentEventHandler::ServerSentEventHandler

    @section serversenteventhandler_relnotes ServerSentEventHandler Release History

    @subsection serversenteventhandler_v1_0_2 Version 1.0.2
    - added supoprt for customizable heartbeat messages to support JSON-RPC requests as heartbeat message in MCP
      server handlers
     (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4958">issue 4958</a>)

    @subsection serversenteventhandler_v1_0_1 Version 1.0.1
    - More flexible SSE handler support

    @subsection serversenteventhandler_v1_0 Version 1.0
    - the initial version of the ServerSentEventHandler module
*/

#! the ServerSentEventHandler namespace contains all the objects in the ServerSentEventHandler module
public namespace ServerSentEventHandler {
}
